oracle_id":"01546b7d-a233-4176-8843-d732074dc5b6","published_at":"2024-11-08","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Battles will enter with double the normal number of defense counters.","oracle_id":"01546b7d-a233-4176-8843-d732074dc5b6","published_at":"2024-11-08","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Everything that is specified by the effect creating the original token or tokens will also be true about the additional token or tokens created by Doubling Season's replacement effect. For example, if an effect tells you to create a token \"tapped and attacking,\" the additional tokens will also be tapped and attacking.","oracle_id":"01546b7d-a233-4176-8843-d732074dc5b6","published_at":"2024-11-08","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Doubling Season affects permanents that enter with counters.","oracle_id":"01546b7d-a233-4176-8843-d732074dc5b6","published_at":"2024-11-08","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Planeswalkers will enter with double the normal number of loyalty counters. However, if you activate an ability whose cost has you put loyalty counters on a planeswalker, the number you put on isn't doubled. This is because those counters are put on as a cost, not as an effect.","oracle_id":"01546b7d-a233-4176-8843-d732074dc5b6","published_at":"2024-11-08","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a creature you control would enter the battlefield with a number of +1/+1 counters on it, it enters with that many plus one instead.","oracle_id":"a1f3da21-af6d-450e-bf0b-985d158418e6","published_at":"2023-09-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If two or more effects attempt to modify how many counters would be put on a creature you control, you choose the order to apply those effects, no matter who controls the sources of those effects.","oracle_id":"a1f3da21-af6d-450e-bf0b-985d158418e6","published_at":"2023-09-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Each additional Hardened Scales you control will increase the number of +1/+1 counters placed on a creature you control by one.","oracle_id":"a1f3da21-af6d-450e-bf0b-985d158418e6","published_at":"2023-09-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"A non-Human creature you control that would enter the battlefield with no +1/+1 counters on it enters with one +1/+1 counter on it.","oracle_id":"fa4afcf7-9cf7-4f67-95b9-1f7fe66bf332","published_at":"2019-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Any other non-Human creatures that enter the battlefield at the same time as Grumgully won't get a +1/+1 counter.","oracle_id":"fa4afcf7-9cf7-4f67-95b9-1f7fe66bf332","published_at":"2019-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a non-Human creature enters the battlefield as a copy of a Human creature, it won't get a +1/+1 counter. Similarly, if a Human enters as a non-Human creature, it will get a +1/+1 counter.","oracle_id":"fa4afcf7-9cf7-4f67-95b9-1f7fe66bf332","published_at":"2019-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a card in your library has {X} in its mana cost, X is considered to be 0.","oracle_id":"10180e2f-90c5-4d41-ba44-16b14948f923","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You can find any number of creature cards, so long as their total mana value is 6 or less. For example, you could find eight creature cards with mana value 0 and three with mana value 2, but you couldn't find two with mana value 4.","oracle_id":"10180e2f-90c5-4d41-ba44-16b14948f923","published_at":"2018-03-16","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Pinned Scryfall originals for the creature subset mana value search"}
